1. Change

  `harness/model-guide/pages/review.html` is the new page. It holds the nav
  links `./real-work.html` and `./review.html`, the review table, the counts
  by class and severity, the passes, the set counts, and the method note.

  `harness/model-guide/preview.sh` gains `--pilot-gate <pass|fail>`. It reads
  the newest score file under `harness/model-guide/data/review-scores/` and
  the public set manifest `harness/model-guide/data/sets/<set_id>.json`. It
  writes `review.html` from `pages/review.html`, and it copies the score
  file to `review.json`. A run with no score file removes a stale review
  page and writes none. `--pilot-gate fail` hides every rank and prints one
  line `preview: pilot gate fail` on stdout.

  The page shows the route row with the rank, the worst, median, and best
  score, the blocker recall as a whole percent, the false claims, and the
  real defects. The false claims, the real defects, and the counts by class
  and severity are sums over the passes of the route. A route with fewer than
  three complete passes shows the word incomplete with dashed score cells. A
  provisional pass keeps its route complete and shows its own state. The
  method note names the set size as `<n> diffs`, the weights 5, 2, and 1, the
  false-claim cost 2, `N = 3`, and the pilot gate. The page and `review.json`
  hold no private field and no private path.

